module kyed-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6 }

// The Eastern District of Kentucky's own civil periods and limits, counted
// under FRCP 6(a), which governs a period stated in a local rule. Stated in
// the rules but not declared: the marshal's thirty working days for service
// of a summons and for a writ of habeas corpus ad testificandum (LR 4.2,
// 83.8) and the seven working days to submit process (LR 4.3), counted in
// working days, for which lit/core has no rule; the 14-day or later
// deadline for a document whose redaction is ordered (LR 5.2), keyed to the
// greater of two periods; the thirty days to refile a pro se or in forma
// pauperis petition on the court's form (LR 5.3), which runs from a
// deficiency order this layer does not model; the nine months without
// action after which the court may order the plaintiff to show cause (LR
// 41.1), which permits a court order and sets no party's deadline; and the
// attorney discipline periods (LR 83.3), which no event of the civil case
// models. No response to an objection to a magistrate judge's order may be
// filed unless the court directs (LR 72.2), so none is declared. The
// earlier E.D. Ky. outline's FRCP flow and its Supreme Court decisions
// (Twombly, Iqbal, Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby, Matsushita, Frow v.
// De La Vega) are FRCP authority and belong to lit/frcp and lit/frap; no
// reporter text is vendored, so they are removed here.
/// A motion or response: at most 25 pages without leave of court (LR
/// 7.1(d)).
limit motion-paper { pages <= 25 cite "E.D. Ky. LR 7.1(d)" } cite "E.D. Ky. LR 7.1(d)"
/// A reply: at most 15 pages without leave of court (LR 7.1(d)).
limit reply-paper { pages <= 15 cite "E.D. Ky. LR 7.1(d)" } cite "E.D. Ky. LR 7.1(d)"

/// A motion for an extension of time, setting forth its reasons and
/// whether the other parties consent, is served (LR 7.1(b)).
event ExtensionMotionServed()
/// A motion is served (LR 7.1(c)).
event MotionServed() paper motion-paper
/// A response opposing a motion is served (LR 7.1(c)).
event ResponseServed() paper motion-paper
/// A reply is filed (LR 7.1(c), (d)).
event ReplyFiled() paper reply-paper
/// A notice of removal is filed (LR 81.1(a)).
event NoticeOfRemovalFiled()
/// The action is removed from state court (LR 81.1(b)).
event ActionRemoved()
/// The compliance date a subpoena served by the United States Marshal
/// specifies (LR 45.1).
event SubpoenaComplianceDate()
/// Judgment is entered (LR 54.3, 54.4).
event JudgmentEntered()
/// A magistrate judge's non-dispositive order is served (LR 72.2).
event MagistrateOrderServed()
/// The Social Security Administration issues its most recent notice of
/// award (LR 83.11(a)).
event NoticeOfAward()
/// A petition for attorney's fees under 42 U.S.C. § 406(b) or
/// § 1383(d)(2)(A) is filed (LR 83.11(a)(2)).
event SocialSecurityFeePetitionFiled()
/// A trial, or a hearing on a motion for judgment or dismissal, is
/// scheduled to begin (LR 83.6).
event TrialOrDispositiveHearingScheduled()

/// LR 7.1(b): absent an agreed order, a response opposing a motion for an
/// extension of time is filed within 7 days of service of the motion.
deadline extension-response-period: 7.days after ExtensionMotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Ky. LR 7.1(b)"
/// LR 7.1(c): unless the court orders otherwise, a party opposing a motion
/// files a response within 21 days of service of the motion; failure to
/// respond timely may be grounds for granting it.
deadline motion-response-period: 21.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Ky. LR 7.1(c)"
/// LR 7.1(c): a party may file a reply within 14 days of service of the
/// response.
deadline motion-reply-period: 14.days after ResponseServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Ky. LR 7.1(c)"
/// LR 81.1(a): within 30 days following the filing of a notice of removal,
/// the removing party files any portion of the state court record it
/// considers relevant that it did not file on removal, with the state court
/// docket sheet.
deadline state-record-period: 30.days after NoticeOfRemovalFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Ky. LR 81.1(a)"
/// LR 81.1(b): a movant who wants the district court to rule on a motion
/// pending in state court at removal refiles it within 14 days after
/// removal; responses and replies then follow LR 7.1.
deadline refiled-motion-period: 14.days after ActionRemoved() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Ky. LR 81.1(b)"
/// LR 45.1: where service of a subpoena by the United States Marshal is
/// permitted, the party presents the subpoena, Form 285 and the fees to the
/// Marshal Service at least fourteen days before the compliance date.
deadline marshal-subpoena-period: 14.days before SubpoenaComplianceDate() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Ky. LR 45.1"
/// LR 54.3: the prevailing party files a bill of costs with the clerk and
/// serves it on each adverse party within thirty days of entry of
/// judgment; costs other than the clerk's are otherwise waived.
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 30.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Ky. LR 54.3"
/// LR 54.4: unless a statute provides otherwise, a motion for attorney's
/// fees and related nontaxable expenses under FRCP 54(d)(2) is filed no
/// later than 30 days after entry of judgment, or they are waived.
deadline fee-motion-period: 30.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Ky. LR 54.4"
/// LR 72.2: subject to any deadline the court sets, a party objecting to a
/// magistrate judge's non-dispositive order files a written objection
/// within fourteen days of service of the order.
deadline magistrate-objection-period: 14.days after MagistrateOrderServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Ky. LR 72.2"
/// LR 83.11(a): claimant's counsel may petition for attorney's fees under
/// 42 U.S.C. § 406(b) or § 1383(d)(2)(A) within 30 days of the date shown on
/// the most recent notice of award (EAJA fees are outside the rule).
deadline social-security-fee-petition-period: 30.days after NoticeOfAward() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Ky. LR 83.11(a)"
/// LR 83.11(a)(2): the United States Attorney or the claimant may respond
/// to the fee petition within 30 days of its filing.
deadline social-security-fee-response-period: 30.days after SocialSecurityFeePetitionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Ky. LR 83.11(a)"
/// LR 83.6: absent leave on a motion showing compelling circumstances, an
/// attorney of record may not withdraw within twenty-one days of trial or
/// a hearing on any motion for judgment or dismissal.
deadline withdrawal-cutoff: 21.days before TrialOrDispositiveHearingScheduled() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Ky. LR 83.6"
